First, can you fix the chat-history refresh. I think it has to do with date changes, so if it is possible to fix the underlying cause that will be helpful.&#x20;

Second, for the phase crossing, I still don't understand why the particular combination arg(q\_{N-1}+iq_N) tells you about the zeros of F, which is the function we care about (presumably).

Finally, for the fixed zero idea, I'm starting to really like the direction here. This gives a natural resolution as N increases. So if two zeros are in the same small ball, then they can't really be resolved. That is not really a problem, that is kind of a "fuzzy" zero collision. It might be the case that understanding the fuzzy zero collisions in the context of the De Bruijn Newman flow can help understand the limit as the resolution tends to zero. It gives kind of an approximate way of understanding zero collisions.
